WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.900
Viserys Targaryen:This world wasn't always
so small and petty.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:11.990
Thousands of years ago, while the rest of
men prayed to gods, the Valyrians became them.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:17.400
Through magic or sheer will, they mastered
the greatest creatures in history.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.470
A horse grants man dominion over the land,
a ship over the sea.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:31.659
But dragons gave us the sky, and everything
and everyone beneath it.

00:00:31.659 --> 00:00:35.850
At its height, my ancestors ruled the known
world.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.500
Whatever parts we didn't weren't worth knowing.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:45.219
Our capital of Valyria shamed the magnificent
cities of the east, for hammers and chisels

00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:49.730
were no match for dragonfire and sorcery.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:56.590
It was a city and an empire built to last
until the end of time.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.949
It didn't.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:02.310
Four hundred years ago, the Doom fell on Valyria.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.480
Mountains cracked open like eggs.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.290
Lakes and rivers boiled.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:13.840
Fountains of fire, ash, and smoke spewed from
the ground, so high and so hot that even dragons

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.910
burned in flight.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.170
The land splintered, and the angry sea rushed
in.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:26.930
In hours, the greatest city in history became
history.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:31.450
But my ancestors didn't burn or drown with
the rest of their race.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:38.880
Twelve years before the Doom, despite the
sneers of his rivals, Aenar Targaryen abandoned

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.820
the capital with his family.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:46.750
Legends claim that his daughter foresaw the
destruction of the city in a dream.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:53.240
More likely, Aenar met with some mishap at
court and chose exile over execution.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:02:00.270
He and House Targaryen slinked away to a dreary,
remote, godforsaken island.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.590
Forsaken no longer.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:10.830
With arts now lost to the world, we transformed
a tiny outpost into Dragonstone, a fortress

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.090
fit for the last Dragonlords.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:19.430
Then Aenar's descendants settled into it like
a tomb for their lost homeland.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.590
Until Aegon.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:28.600
When he looked east, he saw the past: old,
tired, dead.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:37.760
But when he looked west, he saw the future:
gold in the ground, gold in the fields, and

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.569
no dragons in the sky but his.

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:46.040
Varys: Westeros has mighty rivers, but none
of them compare to the Rhoyne.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:51.610
It is said that there is no stream or puddle
in western Essos but drains to Mother Rhoyne.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:55.820
No doubt, an exaggeration.Until one sees the
river.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:00.510
At its widest, a man in the center can't see
a shore to either side.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:05.150
The greatest of Mother Rhoyne's children were
the Rhoynar, a civilization as ancient and

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.840
grand as Old Ghis.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.120
Fishers, traders, scholars, workers of wood,
stone, and metal, the Rhoynar raised their

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:17.160
elegant cities from the headwaters of the
Rhoyne down to her mouth, each lovelier than

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.160
the last.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.530
For many centuries, the Rhoynar lived in relative
peace.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:26.770
When invaders swept down from the hills, the
Rhoynar women and men would don silver-scaled

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:32.060
armor, fish head helms, tall spears, and turtle
shell shields.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.810
If the enemy did not laugh themselves away,
it was said that Mother Rhoyne would whisper

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:42.069
the enemy's secrets to her children, and the
Rhoynish wizards could raise watery walls

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:44.220
to drown their foes.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.990
Whatever magic the Rhoynar may have had, it
wasn't enough.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:52.630
When Valyrian colonists first arrived, the
Rhoynar embraced them, for all men were welcome

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.420
to share the bounty of Mother Rhoyne.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:04:01.209
Perhaps a water people should have been more
cautious of strangers who exulted fire and

00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:02.209
blood.

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:07.190
Legend has it that one day the Valyrians netted
and butchered one of the giant turtles the

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:08.700
Rhoynar held sacred.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:15.200
As a result, thousands were killed or enslaved,
cities and towns were burned, drowned, and

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.200
rebuilt.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.779
In these wars, the Valyrians emerged as victorious
more often than not.

00:04:19.779 --> 00:04:24.960
The princes of the Rhoynish cities, fiercely
proud of their independence, fought alone,

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.370
whilst the Valyrian colonies aided one another.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:33.719
Eventually, the Rhoynish princes ceased their
squabbling and united behind Prince Garin,

00:04:33.719 --> 00:04:40.840
who led the largest army Essos had ever seen
against 100,000 Valyrian colonists, 100 war

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.300
elephants, and three dragonlords.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.699
Thousands burned, but thousands more sheltered
in the shallows of the river whilst the Rhoynish

00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:53.599
wizards raised enormous water spouts against
the foes' dragons.

00:04:53.599 --> 00:05:00.120
Rhoynish archers brought down two of the dragons
whilst the third fled wounded, and thereafter

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.889
the Rhoynar named Garin "the Great."

00:05:02.889 --> 00:05:07.300
But Mother Valyria proved just as caring as
Mother Rhoyne.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:12.960
When Garin the Great marched his army against
Volantis, three hundred Valyrian dragons descended

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.280
from the sky.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.750
Tens of thousands burned whilst others rushed
into the river.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.039
But the fire burned so hot that the waters
boiled and turned to steam.

00:05:22.039 --> 00:05:27.039
Garin the Great was captured alive and made
to watch as Valyrians butchered every last

00:05:27.039 --> 00:05:32.080
man, so many that their blood turned the great
harbor of Volantis red as far as the eye could

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.080
see.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:37.689
Then they forced Garin to watch as they marched
on his own city and enslaved all the women

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:40.490
and children his army had left behind.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:45.550
The singers claimed that Prince Garin called
out Mother Rhoyne to curse the Valyrians,

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:50.210
and she, in turn, flooded the city with foul
waters and a damp fog that caused the skin

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:55.930
of the Valyrians to harden and crack, and
thus was born greyscale.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:06:01.830
Fearing a similar fate, another Rhoynish ruler,
Princess Nymeria, led her own people into

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:06.599
every ship, skiff, and raft they had and fled
Essos.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:12.619
Eventually, after much hardship, they landed
in sunswept and bone dry Dorne.

00:06:12.619 --> 00:06:15.619
But we all know that tale.

00:06:15.619 --> 00:06:20.970
Now Valyria has followed the Rhoynar out of
this world, and her daughters have grown into

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.569
Free Cities, wealthy and powerful and proud.

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:31.349
Still, Mother Rhoyne flows on, past ancient
ruins and bustling harbors, sweeping all man's

00:06:31.349 --> 00:06:33.289
kingdoms to the sea.

00:06:33.289 --> 00:06:39.469
Samwell Tarly:According to legend, House Targaryen
survived the Doom of Valyria thanks to Daenys

00:06:39.469 --> 00:06:43.630
the Dreamer, who foresaw the calamity and
convinced her father to flee their homeland.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.219
It could be true.

00:06:46.219 --> 00:06:48.969
The Targaryens were always a bit more.

00:06:48.969 --> 00:06:54.080
But as Maester Yandel points out, in the East,
the Targaryens were one of a thousand minor

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:58.749
noble families, and in Westeros, they became
kings.

00:06:58.749 --> 00:07:02.740
Politics, not prophecy, could have drawn them
to our shores.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:08.400
Viserys Targaryen: East of Westeros lies the
Smoking Sea, where no ship dares sail.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:14.369
There are those who swear it to be demon-haunted,
and who's to say they're wrong?

00:07:14.369 --> 00:07:20.009
For it was there, thousands of years ago,
that a cataclysmic event occurred, destroying

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:23.949
one of the great civilizations in history.

00:07:23.949 --> 00:07:29.439
The precise details of their origins are lost
to us, but it is said the Valyrians were once

00:07:29.439 --> 00:07:34.629
a modest community of shepherds, tending their
flocks on a small peninsula of the great eastern

00:07:34.629 --> 00:07:37.039
continent.

00:07:37.039 --> 00:07:43.250
One fateful day, in a volcanic area known
as the Fourteen Fires, they made a shattering

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:44.279
discovery.

00:07:44.279 --> 00:07:45.309
Dragons.

00:07:45.309 --> 00:07:53.849
They were monstrous, scaled creatures, with
massive wings, sharp claws, and fiery breath.

00:07:53.849 --> 00:07:58.469
They were also said to have a deep-rooted
connection to magic.

00:07:58.469 --> 00:08:02.979
In time, the Valyrians were able to tame the
beasts.

00:08:02.979 --> 00:08:09.069
Harnessing their immense power, they established
a city of wonder unlike any before or since.

00:08:09.069 --> 00:08:15.569
They became skilled at sorcery and metallurgy,
creating uncommon weapons of spell-forged

00:08:15.569 --> 00:08:17.119
steel.

00:08:17.119 --> 00:08:22.060
Wielding these weapons astride their dragons,
the Valyrians conquered the surrounding lands

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.870
and slowly expanded west.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:31.139
At the time, the Ghiscari Empire dominated
much of the great eastern continent and tried

00:08:31.139 --> 00:08:34.029
to stop Valyria's expansion.

00:08:34.029 --> 00:08:39.130
The Ghiscari legions attacked the Valyrians
five times, but could never defeat them.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:45.839
Finally, the Valyrians marched on their capital,
Old Ghis, and obliterated it, turning its

00:08:45.839 --> 00:08:51.819
streets and buildings to ash with dragon flame,
and wiping the Ghiscari people and their culture

00:08:51.819 --> 00:08:54.759
off the face of the earth.

00:08:54.759 --> 00:08:59.649
The Freehold of Valyria, as it came to be
known, became the most advanced civilization

00:08:59.649 --> 00:09:04.560
in the known world, with its own language,
gods, and culture.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:10.370
The Valyrians' reach extended far and wide,
covering most of the continent.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:16.529
Great cities were built and roadways paved,
all of which led back to Valyria.

00:09:16.529 --> 00:09:21.750
The Freehold would prosper for nearly five
thousand years.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.050
But it was not to last.

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:29.949
An event that became known only as the Doom
laid waste to the Valyrians, their capital

00:09:29.949 --> 00:09:32.829
city, and its surrounding lands.

00:09:32.829 --> 00:09:38.759
The peninsula itself was shattered, becoming
what is now the Smoking Sea.

00:09:38.759 --> 00:09:44.180
Every dragon was thought to be lost, as were
the Valyrians' spells, knowledge, and recorded

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.029
history.

00:09:46.029 --> 00:09:49.870
Thus the mighty empire collapsed.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.720
What caused this cataclysm?

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:54.980
No one knows for certain.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.949
Some say it was a volcanic eruption.

00:09:57.949 --> 00:10:00.990
Others say the Valyrians' own sorcery got
the better of them.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:08.190
In any event, the Doom's devastation of the
Valyrian people was total with the exception

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:13.089
of a small rocky island in the Narrow Sea.

00:10:13.089 --> 00:10:14.480
Dragonstone.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:19.980
For it was there that the Targaryens, the
last of Old Valyria, dwelled.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:24.431
They would lie in wait for another hundred
years before unleashing the fury of the dragon

00:10:24.431 --> 00:10:26.310
on another continent.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.510
Westeros.

